hls: a playlist load cut short or failing half way fails, and drops its connection

With http_persistent (the default) a playlist reload reuses the
connection the last load read its answer on. A load that failed before
the end of the answer (a garbled line, which 0102 plays through on a
live reload) left the rest of that answer unread on the connection, and
the next reload read it first: no "#EXTM3U" line, so that reload failed
too, and so on, a line of the old answer at a time (in the fixture, three
garbled answers made 13 failed reloads).

A read that ended in an error was no failure at all: the line loop ends
at avio_feof(), which an error sets as the end does, so an answer cut by
the server (EIO since 0107) or interrupted by the caller's callback (a
seek during a reload) was taken whole. The truncated list replaced the
playlist until the next reload, and an interrupted connection kept the
rest of the answer for the next one.

Fail such a load with the read's error, so the previous list stays
(0071) and 0102 decides what follows (an interrupt returns; a cut is
retried), and close the kept-alive connection when a load fails; the
next load opens a new one.

A read that ended in an error inside the first line failed as INVALIDDATA
(no "#EXTM3U"): it fails with the read's error too. And an interrupted
load stamped last_load_time as any load does, so the next reload, or the
refresh of the seek that interrupted it, waited a reload interval and
resolved on the old list: an AVERROR_EXIT load is no load and stamps
nothing.

diff --git a/libavformat/hls.c b/libavformat/hls.c
--- a/libavformat/hls.c
+++ b/libavformat/hls.c
@@ -1167,7 +1167,8 @@ static int parse_playlist(HLSContext *c, const char *url,
 
     ff_get_chomp_line(in, line, sizeof(line));
     if (strcmp(line, "#EXTM3U")) {
-        ret = AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
+        /* a first line cut short by an interrupt or the server is that error */
+        ret = in->error < 0 ? in->error : AVERROR_INVALIDDATA;
         goto fail;
     }
 
@@ -1445,6 +1446,13 @@ static int parse_playlist(HLSContext *c, const char *url,
             }
         }
     }
+    /* The lines end with an error as with the end of the answer: a read
+     * cut short (an interrupt, a body cut by the server) is no whole
+     * playlist. The previous list stays, the connection is dropped below. */
+    if (in->error < 0) {
+        ret = in->error;
+        goto fail;
+    }
     if (prev_segments && pls->anchor_ts != AV_NOPTS_VALUE &&
         pls->anchor_seq_no < pls->start_seq_no) {
         /* Carry the anchor to the new first segment through the segments the
@@ -1502,7 +1510,9 @@ fail:
         pls->finished        = prev_finished;
         pls->type            = prev_type;
     }
-    if (pls) {
+    /* An interrupted load is none: the next read or a seek's refresh loads
+     * again at once, not a reload interval later from the old list */
+    if (pls && ret != AVERROR_EXIT) {
         pls->last_load_time = load_start;
         if (ret >= 0)
             pls->reload_error_time = 0;
@@ -1510,6 +1520,10 @@ fail:
     av_free(new_url);
     if (close_in)
         ff_format_io_close(c->ctx, &in);
+    else if (ret < 0 && in && in == *playlist_pb)
+        /* a load that failed half way left the rest of the answer on the
+         * kept-alive connection, which the next load would read first */
+        ff_format_io_close(c->ctx, playlist_pb);
     c->ctx->ctx_flags = c->ctx->ctx_flags & ~(unsigned)AVFMTCTX_UNSEEKABLE;
     if (!c->n_variants || !c->variants[0]->n_playlists ||
         !c->variants[0]->playlists[0]->n_segments)
